mutants/

# Downloaded primary sources are large and re-fetchable; the manifest pins them.
Accounting_Brain/Evidence_Library/sources/*.pdf

# Agent worktrees and local session state. Never repository content.
#
# `.claude/*` and NOT `.claude/` — the trailing-slash form excludes the
# DIRECTORY, and git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is
# excluded, so every negation below would have been silently dead. Measured:
# `git add .claude/settings.json` refused with "ignored by one of your
# .gitignore files" until this line lost its slash.
.claude/*

# EXCEPT the enforcement mechanism, which IS repository content.
#
# MEASURED 2026-08-06, and this line was the single point of failure: with
# `.claude/` ignored wholesale, `git ls-files .claude/` returned NOTHING. Every
# hook enforcing this project's engineering rules lived in `~/.claude/` on one
# laptop. A fresh clone, a second machine or a wiped home directory got zero
# enforcement, and the rules survived only because one person's home directory
# happened to still exist.
#
# `settings.json` and `hooks/` are therefore un-ignored deliberately. Everything
# else under `.claude/` — worktrees above all — stays ignored.
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/hooks/**
